  "_doc": [
    "Calibration for the correlated cross-asset factor simulator (ADR-0026).",
    "Factor order everywhere: [EQUITY, RATES_LEVEL, RATES_SLOPE, USD].",
    "Hand-curated from long-run market statistics (2015-2024 era): equity factor ~16% ann vol",
    "(S&P 500), USD factor ~7% (DXY), rates level ~5bp/day (US 10Y), slope ~2bp/day (2s10s).",
    "Single-name vols/betas are their well-known long-run values. Correlations are per regime:",
    "RISK_OFF = flight to quality (stocks down, yields down => bond futures UP, USD bid,",
    "correlations tighten); INFLATION_SHOCK = the 2022 pattern (stocks down WHILE yields up,",
    "stock-bond correlation flips sign). Treasury futures (ZT/ZF/ZN/ZB) and swaps carry no spec:",
    "they price FROM the curve, whose level/slope ARE the RATES factors.",
    "Refresh from real daily history with: python3 scripts/calibrate_sim.py (needs internet;",
    "run on the Pi). The platform itself never fetches at runtime (ADR-0009)."
  ],
